WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.920
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:01.190 --> 00:02.293
Ji?

3
00:03.470 --> 00:04.901
Ji, is that you?

4
00:05.454 --> 00:08.516
Wow, you’re all grown up.

5
00:09.105 --> 00:11.970
(You knew Ruth before, Ji?)

6
00:12.320 --> 00:14.218
How come you never told me that?

7
00:14.625 --> 00:16.676
Why does it say ‘Theeraruth’?

8
00:16.945 --> 00:18.670
Isn’t his name Atiwitch?

9
00:19.120 --> 00:20.120
It’s a long story.

10
00:38.280 --> 00:40.000
Ji! Ji!

11
00:40.050 --> 00:41.323
- Ji, baby! - Ji!

12
00:44.250 --> 00:46.058
- Oh. - I know the truth.

13
00:46.465 --> 00:47.309
Aren’t you mad?

14
00:47.360 --> 00:49.127
You never came to me and said hi.

15
00:49.403 --> 00:50.945
And I forgot all about us.

16
00:50.974 --> 00:51.974
Let’s call it even.

17
00:54.720 --> 00:57.120
Now that my parents know we’re friends again,

18
00:58.320 --> 01:00.029
they want you to come over for dinner.

19
01:00.680 --> 01:01.680
Good evening.

20
01:01.760 --> 01:02.821
Good evening.

21
01:03.287 --> 01:05.280
My mom and dad wanted me to give you this.

22
01:13.500 --> 01:14.981
I’m Kwan from Class 2.

23
01:15.163 --> 01:17.025
You know Kwan?

24
01:17.534 --> 01:17.970
Yeah.

25
01:18.138 --> 01:19.280
The drama club president.

26
02:56.029 --> 02:57.229
YELLOW TIGER

27
02:57.243 --> 02:58.836
(PURPLE SCORPION)

28
02:58.872 --> 03:00.130
(BLUE SHARK)

29
03:02.980 --> 03:04.458
Sorry. Excuse me.

30
03:04.494 --> 03:07.083
- Sorry. - Sorry. Sorry.

31
03:13.541 --> 03:14.036
There.

32
03:14.494 --> 03:15.494
Okay.

33
03:15.694 --> 03:17.650
- Need any more help? - No, that’s all.

34
03:18.043 --> 03:19.650
You’re free until the parade’s over.

35
03:20.632 --> 03:21.632
- Let’s go. - Let’s go.

36
03:22.218 --> 03:24.436
- Grilled pork. - Let’s get grilled pork.

37
03:29.830 --> 03:32.021
Would you like a zodiac reading?

38
03:33.258 --> 03:34.283
Let’s do this one.

39
03:34.312 --> 03:36.392
Arrange the flower, leaf,

40
03:36.429 --> 03:38.196
mountain, and sun in your preferred order.

41
03:38.660 --> 03:39.840
(Hmm...)

42
03:40.050 --> 03:43.512
(The sun, leaf, mountain, flower.)

43
03:43.534 --> 03:45.861
The sun, leaf, mountain, flower.

44
03:46.341 --> 03:48.218
Okay, let me read it for you.

45
03:48.516 --> 03:50.167
Your fortune says...

46
03:50.196 --> 03:52.690
Your relationship with him is like a lemon.

47
03:52.727 --> 03:55.214
Sweet and sour, fizzy, and refreshing.

48
03:55.694 --> 03:57.789
Your love life is so enviable right now that

49
03:57.818 --> 03:59.469
single people would be jealous.

50
04:00.380 --> 04:03.578
But beware of the bitter taste of the lemon peel.

51
04:03.600 --> 04:06.072
That person is keeping a secret from you.

52
04:21.200 --> 04:25.890
NAWINA SCHOOL

53
04:25.934 --> 04:28.421
Ji, about the lunch boxes…

54
04:34.930 --> 04:38.109
Oh, my mom said she’ll drop them off in front of the school.

55
04:38.840 --> 04:41.490
You can pay after the budget has been approved.

56
04:43.380 --> 04:44.380
Are you okay?

57
04:45.018 --> 04:46.152
Is there something wrong?

58
04:47.510 --> 04:48.356
Nothing.

59
04:48.400 --> 04:50.360
We’ve brought the bottled waters since yesterday.

60
04:55.985 --> 04:57.454
Shouldn’t you be at the competition?

61
04:59.280 --> 05:00.552
We’re leaving at 7.

62
05:00.596 --> 05:01.596
I’ll be gone soon.

63
05:03.380 --> 05:05.243
I probably won’t see you again today.

64
05:06.340 --> 05:07.876
Have fun on the Sports Day.

65
05:13.869 --> 05:15.860
I’m off now.

66
05:16.341 --> 05:17.341
Mmm.

67
05:17.490 --> 05:18.490
Good luck.

68
05:30.220 --> 05:31.220
Jeez!

69
05:32.040 --> 05:33.040
What are you looking at?

70
05:33.600 --> 05:34.600
Nothing.

71
05:35.050 --> 05:36.050
“Good luck.”

72
05:43.500 --> 05:44.792
Here, Ji.

73
05:44.843 --> 05:45.843
Thank you.

74
05:46.014 --> 05:47.076
Where’s Ty?

75
05:47.374 --> 05:49.032
Oh, he has an upset stomach.

76
05:49.061 --> 05:50.579
He ate too much grilled pork with sticky rice.

77
05:50.603 --> 05:52.014
- Poor boy. - Oh.

78
05:52.080 --> 05:54.654
Being sick on the Sports Day.

79
05:55.272 --> 05:57.105
I’ll go, then.

80
05:57.483 --> 05:58.901
Thank you. See you later.

81
05:58.938 --> 06:00.545
Bye-bye. See you later.

82
06:01.210 --> 06:01.658
Go.

83
06:01.890 --> 06:02.890
Let’s go, honey.

84
06:04.430 --> 06:06.058
Can’t you sing louder?

85
06:06.094 --> 06:07.294
Don’t you see the other teams?

86
06:07.520 --> 06:09.641
We didn’t ask you to come practice during your school break.

87
06:09.665 --> 06:11.401
We’ve prepared free food and drinks for you.

88
06:11.425 --> 06:12.734
We’re not doing any formations.

89
06:13.098 --> 06:15.018
All you have to do is sit there, sing, and clap.

90
06:15.381 --> 06:16.821
Why can’t you even do that properly?

91
06:17.700 --> 06:18.880
Next, we’ll practice…

92
06:18.916 --> 06:20.456
You’ve been practicing since this morning.

93
06:20.480 --> 06:21.560
Why don’t you take a break?

94
06:23.320 --> 06:25.360
- But... - You can take a break and have some water.

95
06:25.760 --> 06:27.880
The kids might faint during the cheering competition.

96
06:31.560 --> 06:33.687
Ten-minute break! Don’t leave the stands.

97
06:40.520 --> 06:41.716
Here are your drinks.

98
06:42.276 --> 06:43.432
Pass them along.

99
06:46.109 --> 06:47.109
Thank you.

100
06:48.950 --> 06:50.710
You volunteered to be the cheer squad leader

101
06:51.490 --> 06:54.450
because you didn't like being yelled at by your seniors in Grade 7, right?

102
06:57.860 --> 06:58.860
Yeah.

103
07:00.356 --> 07:01.356
You're right.

104
07:03.800 --> 07:07.120
My parents have just allowed me to participate in school activities.

105
07:07.910 --> 07:10.581
I saw how hard the other teams were working,

106
07:10.618 --> 07:13.549
so I... wanted to beat them.

107
07:14.830 --> 07:15.830
Thank you.

108
07:17.010 --> 07:18.010
Mmm.

109
07:18.196 --> 07:19.621
Oww!

110
07:19.672 --> 07:21.687
- Ji, The Good Boy. - Stop it.

111
07:21.716 --> 07:23.585
- Ji, The Good Boy. - That’s enough.

112
07:25.320 --> 07:27.000
The school nurse told me to get some rest.

113
07:27.170 --> 07:28.170
But I’m just so strong.

114
07:28.814 --> 07:30.614
I felt better as soon as I took the medicine.

115
07:35.860 --> 07:37.258
Hold on, Ji. Here it comes again.

116
07:40.370 --> 07:41.432
Do you need any help?

117
07:41.461 --> 07:43.672
No, thank you. I’m almost done.

118
07:43.694 --> 07:45.214
- You should help them instead. - Okay.

119
07:50.340 --> 07:51.890
I told you I’m good.

120
07:52.240 --> 07:53.240
You should…

121
07:56.730 --> 07:58.065
Hello, ma’am.

122
07:58.843 --> 07:59.890
How are you doing?

123
08:00.740 --> 08:02.020
Aren’t you afraid of me anymore?

124
08:02.909 --> 08:05.578
Now you're brave because you have someone backing you up, huh?

125
08:07.690 --> 08:10.356
Could you tell Ms. Mai

126
08:10.865 --> 08:13.360
that my classmates really liked the extra worksheets?

127
08:13.912 --> 08:15.432
Could she make some more for us?

128
08:18.400 --> 08:19.480
Would you like some drinks?

129
08:21.090 --> 08:22.712
I can’t stand a kid like you.

130
08:23.010 --> 08:24.710
I’m not your biggest fan, either.

131
08:35.210 --> 08:37.127
Are they having fun down there?

132
08:37.149 --> 08:39.539
Your favorite student, Jiraphat, asked me to tell you he loved your worksheets.

133
08:39.563 --> 08:40.563
Are you happy?

134
08:42.320 --> 08:45.883
You should know that wasn’t what he meant.

135
08:47.700 --> 08:49.432
Perceptive kid like him

136
08:49.469 --> 08:51.607
must know you're the one who made those worksheets.

137
09:18.980 --> 09:21.840
Say cheese. Okay.

138
09:21.876 --> 09:23.425
A candid shot.

139
09:23.950 --> 09:25.294
Yeah, yeah. That’s good.

140
09:25.323 --> 09:26.443
One-finger pose.

141
09:29.410 --> 09:30.887
That’s a good one.

142
09:30.923 --> 09:31.418
YELLOW TIGER, BLUE SHARK,

143
09:31.447 --> 09:32.516
PURPLE SCORPION Hey, Gun.

144
09:33.440 --> 09:34.840
You did great getting second place.

145
09:35.498 --> 09:36.523
Hey, hey.

146
09:36.550 --> 09:38.909
Oww, oww, oww.

147
09:38.938 --> 09:40.050
I was praising him.

148
09:40.072 --> 09:41.789
Why are you sitting on me, Ji?

149
09:41.818 --> 09:42.818
Ji!

150
09:43.229 --> 09:46.196
- Oww! Oh, god. - Oh!

151
09:46.240 --> 09:47.360
Oww, oww, oww!

152
09:47.389 --> 09:48.567
- Oww, oww! - Oww! Help!

153
09:48.596 --> 09:50.116
- Help me! - Oww!

154
09:50.632 --> 09:51.723
Oww, oww!

155
09:52.620 --> 09:53.620
What are you guys doing?

156
09:55.040 --> 09:56.040
Down.

157
09:59.309 --> 10:00.414
Umm, sir…

158
10:00.749 --> 10:02.625
Could you take a picture for us?

159
10:03.720 --> 10:05.476
- Fine. - With my brand-new phone.

160
10:07.040 --> 10:07.956
Is the camera on?

161
10:07.985 --> 10:09.490
- 1... 2... 3. - Say cheese.

162
10:09.520 --> 10:10.960
Oh, my hands were shaking. One more.

163
10:11.105 --> 10:12.105
1…

164
10:13.030 --> 10:14.109
Body shot.

165
10:14.407 --> 10:15.221
Nice!

166
10:15.250 --> 10:16.327
1…2…

167
10:16.370 --> 10:17.370
Kissing pose.

168
10:18.930 --> 10:19.930
Look like a monkey.

169
10:20.138 --> 10:21.665
- You mean us? - Just you.

170
10:21.694 --> 10:22.694
You, too.

171
10:23.220 --> 10:25.294
See? I took that one.

172
10:26.680 --> 10:27.680
You like it?

173
10:28.840 --> 10:29.912
The foreground is so blurry.

174
10:29.934 --> 10:31.174
None of the pictures are clear.

175
10:31.636 --> 10:33.276
You didn't get any good shots of us, sir.

176
10:34.260 --> 10:37.280
It looks like you took these with a calculator, not a phone.

177
10:38.960 --> 10:40.450
Ouch!

178
10:40.487 --> 10:42.210
One for each of you.

179
10:45.730 --> 10:47.370
YELLOW TIGER, BLUE SHARK, PURPLE SCORPION

180
10:49.130 --> 10:51.490
Who will represent the Blue Team in the eating race?

181
10:51.716 --> 10:53.323
Me, me, me.

182
11:03.345 --> 11:04.345
3…

183
11:04.770 --> 11:05.770
2…

184
11:06.130 --> 11:07.130
1.

185
11:10.580 --> 11:11.580
Swallow it.

186
11:12.392 --> 11:13.392
Swallow it.

187
11:14.290 --> 11:15.760
Come on, Tyler.

188
11:19.760 --> 11:21.338
Tyler! Tyler!

189
11:27.500 --> 11:30.421
Go, go, go, go.

190
11:30.465 --> 11:32.356
Tyler! Tyler! Tyler! Tyler!

191
11:44.312 --> 11:46.276
Woo!

192
11:46.312 --> 11:50.349
(Next up is the three-legged race.)

193
11:50.567 --> 11:54.065
(Please send your representatives within 15 minutes.)

194
11:54.632 --> 11:57.767
Who wants to represent us in the three-legged race? Raise your hand.

195
11:58.560 --> 12:01.520
Stop right there, Tyler. The three-legged race is a team event.

196
12:01.861 --> 12:03.869
You only have one competition slot left.

197
12:03.898 --> 12:05.378
You should compete in something else.

198
12:05.527 --> 12:06.836
Who else, then?

199
12:11.620 --> 12:12.620
I’ll do it.

200
12:14.770 --> 12:16.865
I’ll go with Ji.

201
12:16.894 --> 12:18.860
Okay. Jiraphat and Tawan, then.

202
12:20.780 --> 12:23.090
- Break a leg! - Woo!

203
12:25.830 --> 12:26.830
Sign here.

204
12:30.100 --> 12:31.100
Umm...

205
12:31.309 --> 12:32.580
There are ten minutes left.

206
12:32.720 --> 12:34.065
You can wait at the starting point.

207
12:34.087 --> 12:35.087
I’ll be there.

208
13:05.520 --> 13:06.520
Is this okay?

209
13:19.280 --> 13:20.280
What’s up, my friend?

210
13:23.530 --> 13:24.530
Hi...

211
13:24.756 --> 13:25.756
My friend.

212
13:29.590 --> 13:30.950
But once we cross the finish line,

213
13:32.780 --> 13:34.100
we won't be just friends anymore.

214
13:44.840 --> 13:45.840
Ready?

215
13:46.792 --> 13:47.792
3…

216
13:50.160 --> 13:51.160
2…

217
13:53.780 --> 13:54.780
1.

218
14:48.090 --> 14:55.469
Woohoo!

219
15:00.870 --> 15:02.436
Class President, can we talk?

220
15:13.940 --> 15:15.585
Woo!

221
15:15.607 --> 15:16.607
Well done.

222
15:17.580 --> 15:18.378
Well done.

223
15:18.407 --> 15:19.549
Nice job, Ji.

224
15:19.621 --> 15:21.287
That’s my brother.

225
15:21.534 --> 15:23.054
Another medal for Blue Team.

226
15:23.083 --> 15:24.465
We’re getting the big trophy.

227
15:24.501 --> 15:26.189
I know that’s right.

228
15:27.540 --> 15:29.020
(But once we cross the finish line, )

229
15:31.800 --> 15:33.192
we won't be just friends anymore.

230
15:35.380 --> 15:38.989
(We won't be just friends anymore.)

231
15:42.580 --> 15:44.283
Yay!

232
15:47.240 --> 15:51.650
- Yay! - Yay!

233
15:51.680 --> 15:55.512
Yay!

234
16:07.340 --> 16:08.340
What’s the matter?

235
16:13.140 --> 16:14.140
Nothing.

236
16:24.280 --> 16:25.316
Drama Club?

237
16:27.890 --> 16:28.952
The event is in January.

238
16:29.345 --> 16:30.745
We’ll start right after Sports Day.

239
16:36.880 --> 16:38.123
Is that your friend, Tyler?

240
16:39.207 --> 16:40.207
Yeah.

241
16:40.378 --> 16:41.378
Why did you ask?

242
16:43.470 --> 16:44.470
Nothing.

243
16:50.000 --> 16:52.654
Yay!!

244
16:52.698 --> 16:54.269
Woo!

245
16:54.290 --> 16:55.789
Good job, Tyler!

246
17:09.780 --> 17:13.912
We gather here together...

247
17:25.050 --> 17:27.425
Look, Ji. Doggie weenie sausages.

248
17:34.390 --> 17:35.752
Crab sticks are ready.

249
17:35.781 --> 17:37.774
- Get them while they’re hot. - I’ll be back.

250
17:50.260 --> 17:51.323
The student council room.

251
17:52.460 --> 17:53.898
I mean the president.

252
17:53.927 --> 17:55.247
He’s at the student council room.

253
17:55.803 --> 17:56.803
Ji.

254
17:57.670 --> 17:58.950
You want some fried crab sticks?

255
18:03.790 --> 18:05.869
You go. I’ll take it from here.

256
18:20.510 --> 18:22.647
- Oh. - Tyler, hi.

257
18:22.683 --> 18:23.912
Hello, Lita.

258
18:23.992 --> 18:24.992
Where did Ji go?

259
18:25.090 --> 18:26.654
Oh, he went to the bathroom.

260
18:26.698 --> 18:27.698
Oh.

261
18:29.140 --> 18:30.538
Can I ask you something?

262
18:30.792 --> 18:31.287
Of course.

263
18:31.310 --> 18:35.316
Which do you like better, crab sticks or sausages?

264
18:35.505 --> 18:37.985
It has to be... crab sticks.

265
18:38.327 --> 18:39.425
They're the best.

266
18:39.600 --> 18:41.869
Even though I know they're not made from real crab,

267
18:42.218 --> 18:43.687
I still eat them every day.

268
18:53.990 --> 18:54.990
Hey.

269
18:57.380 --> 18:58.749
How was the Science competition?

270
18:59.578 --> 19:00.578
It’s the same.

271
19:05.000 --> 19:06.552
You mean you won again?

272
19:12.730 --> 19:14.574
Here, want some?

273
19:43.190 --> 19:44.190
Tyler.

274
19:44.734 --> 19:45.734
Oh, hi, Ploy.

275
19:46.610 --> 19:48.305
This is Kwan.

276
19:50.021 --> 19:51.581
You haven’t joined any clubs, have you?

277
19:53.840 --> 19:54.981
So...

278
19:56.320 --> 19:58.821
Will you audition for the lead role in the school play for me?

279
20:03.418 --> 20:09.700
DRAMA CLUB CASTING LIST, LEAD ROLE RUTH ATIWITCH GRADE 11/1, TYLER GRADE 11/7

280
20:11.890 --> 20:14.058
Don’t you have to go on stage?

281
20:16.700 --> 20:18.000
You want to hear me sing?

282
20:19.770 --> 20:20.770
Can I?

283
20:23.060 --> 20:24.545
Let’s leave that to Tawan.

284
20:34.380 --> 20:36.180
But if you want to hear me sing just for you,

285
20:36.580 --> 20:37.580
you can.

286
20:39.380 --> 20:40.380
I’d love to.

287
20:53.080 --> 21:00.756
MONDAY, NOVEMBER 8, 2010

288
21:43.840 --> 21:45.083
What I said this afternoon,

289
21:45.541 --> 21:47.570
you know what it meant, right?

290
21:51.090 --> 21:52.458
(To me, he is Ruth.)

291
21:53.620 --> 21:55.192
(The actual Ruth.)

292
21:56.010 --> 21:58.829
(I don’t even see him as Theeraruth, my childhood friend.)

293
22:00.890 --> 22:04.065
(I don’t even think about Ruth Atiwitch, the superstar.)

294
22:08.500 --> 22:12.523
(If I let this relationship happen today, )

295
22:13.520 --> 22:14.858
(when that day comes…)

296
22:22.350 --> 22:23.350
Don’t worry.

297
22:24.090 --> 22:25.090
Just trust me.

298
22:37.090 --> 22:38.916
I won the science project competition.

299
22:39.940 --> 22:40.940
Where’s my reward?

300
22:45.000 --> 22:48.443
And I… just won a three-legged race, too.

301
22:51.980 --> 22:53.512
So we’re both winners.

302
22:56.020 --> 22:57.020
I guess so.

303
23:13.723 --> 23:15.992
It’s you who came into my life

304
23:16.036 --> 23:18.720
You light up my new beginning

305
23:18.756 --> 23:22.923
Because of you, I want to keep going

306
23:43.090 --> 23:44.090
Hello?

307
23:44.690 --> 23:45.690
(Wake up.)

308
23:47.160 --> 23:48.160
I’m up.

309
23:54.450 --> 23:55.450
What’s going on?

310
23:55.898 --> 23:56.898
Nothing.

311
23:57.403 --> 23:58.963
Just wanted to give you a wake-up call.

312
24:01.510 --> 24:02.510
Good morning.

313
24:05.360 --> 24:06.360
Good morning.

314
24:06.909 --> 24:08.869
(You don’t need to have breakfast at home today.)

315
24:09.301 --> 24:10.960
(I had my housemaid prepare one for you.)

316
24:11.905 --> 24:12.960
You did that for me?

317
24:13.280 --> 24:14.280
Yeah.

318
24:14.341 --> 24:15.661
So we can eat breakfast together.

319
24:21.900 --> 24:22.960
Together?

320
24:25.410 --> 24:26.410
Um..

321
24:26.500 --> 24:27.500
Yeah.

322
24:28.080 --> 24:29.080
(See you, then.)

323
24:29.440 --> 24:30.440
See you.

324
24:46.690 --> 24:49.454
NAWINA SCHOOL

325
24:54.770 --> 24:55.770
Morning.

326
24:57.330 --> 24:57.883
Hi.

327
24:58.330 --> 24:59.330
Hi.

328
24:59.890 --> 25:02.261
Here. From Ms. Narumon.

329
25:02.312 --> 25:03.520
Your favorite desserts.

330
25:05.390 --> 25:06.390
Hey.

331
25:06.581 --> 25:07.701
Breakfast first.

332
25:11.460 --> 25:12.460
“Breakfast first.”

333
25:12.981 --> 25:13.981
What is it?

334
25:14.494 --> 25:15.494
- Nothing. - Nothing.

335
25:32.341 --> 25:34.340
Will you have dinner at my house after school?

336
25:35.990 --> 25:37.430
My mom and Peach wanted you to come.

337
25:37.658 --> 25:38.658
My dad’s not home.

338
25:45.320 --> 25:48.552
Who is this product being made for? TUESDAY, DECEMBER 7, 2010

339
25:48.581 --> 25:50.065
Okay, everyone. Any questions?

340
25:54.458 --> 25:56.407
Okay, okay. That’s all for today.

341
25:56.538 --> 25:58.400
Attention, students.

342
25:58.436 --> 26:01.003
Thank you.

343
26:01.040 --> 26:01.541
Okay.

344
26:02.030 --> 26:03.665
- Let’s go, Ji. - And don’t forget to…

345
26:07.240 --> 26:09.687
Don't forget to review your lessons, guys.

346
26:12.440 --> 26:15.214
SCHOOL CO-OP

347
26:15.243 --> 26:16.243
I’m back.

348
26:16.620 --> 26:17.410
Come on. Have a seat.

349
26:17.440 --> 26:18.440
Okay.

350
26:19.767 --> 26:20.767
Wow.

351
26:21.447 --> 26:23.163
You need to eat some vegetables.

352
26:25.040 --> 26:26.040
That’s enough.

353
26:34.330 --> 26:35.330
When did this happen?

354
26:35.920 --> 26:37.229
After or before Sports Day?

355
26:42.940 --> 26:43.940
Umm…

356
26:44.749 --> 26:45.890
After Sports Day.

357
26:47.420 --> 26:48.420
I won.

358
26:51.440 --> 26:54.952
You all owe me a milk crepe with extra whipped cream.

359
26:55.236 --> 26:56.236
Yeah, yeah.

360
26:59.060 --> 27:01.105
Hey, don’t worry.

361
27:01.381 --> 27:02.530
The others don’t know yet.

362
27:02.785 --> 27:03.890
We won’t tell.

363
27:05.890 --> 27:07.743
You said the same thing about Jiraphat, the good boy.

364
27:07.767 --> 27:08.767
Come on.

365
27:09.003 --> 27:10.232
I mean it this time.

366
27:10.429 --> 27:11.429
Okay?

367
27:11.781 --> 27:12.781
Promise.

368
27:13.672 --> 27:14.349
- I promise, too. - I promise, too.

369
27:14.370 --> 27:15.505
- Promise. - Promise.

370
27:15.745 --> 27:16.905
- I promise, too. - I promise.

371
27:18.820 --> 27:20.203
Come on. Make a promise.

372
27:20.661 --> 27:21.837
- We won’t tell anyone. - Come on.

373
27:21.861 --> 27:23.760
-Come on, -I’m not telling anyone.

374
27:23.796 --> 27:24.785
Yeah.

375
27:24.810 --> 27:25.978
Promise!

376
27:26.029 --> 27:27.120
- Yay! - Quiet.

377
27:29.600 --> 27:31.192
Now Class 7 has another couple.

378
27:31.483 --> 27:32.756
I'm in Class 7, too.

379
27:33.112 --> 27:34.349
Why can't I get a boyfriend?

380
27:34.370 --> 27:35.520
So jealous.

381
27:35.570 --> 27:36.570
Another couple?

382
27:36.923 --> 27:39.294
Yeah. Gun and Thiti.

383
27:41.316 --> 27:42.316
- Huh?! - Huh?!

384
27:42.552 --> 27:43.552
Come on.

385
27:44.790 --> 27:46.472
Since middle school.

386
27:46.501 --> 27:48.705
All you guys care about is egg yolk ice-cream.

387
27:48.741 --> 27:51.214
Stop eating and pay attention to the others.

388
27:51.905 --> 27:54.050
- Did you know about this, Kong? - Of course.

389
27:55.280 --> 27:56.280
How did you know?

390
27:59.700 --> 28:01.229
Ahem.

391
28:01.272 --> 28:02.272
Listen.

392
28:03.090 --> 28:06.734
I’ve known for a while that Gun and Thiti were dating.

393
28:07.054 --> 28:08.509
Once other people found out,

394
28:08.836 --> 28:10.770
their classmates started teasing them.

395
28:10.792 --> 28:11.738
Mmm.

396
28:11.767 --> 28:15.701
Then word got around to a conservative teacher.

397
28:16.560 --> 28:19.723
Gun and Thiti were called to the discipline office,

398
28:21.330 --> 28:22.589
even though this school doesn't even

399
28:22.610 --> 28:24.341
have a rule against dating.

400
28:24.370 --> 28:25.498
- Mmm. - Mmm, that’s true.

401
28:28.690 --> 28:31.665
Then their parents came to the discipline office

402
28:31.694 --> 28:33.323
and yelled at that teacher.

403
28:33.890 --> 28:35.890
In the end, the teacher gave in.

404
28:35.920 --> 28:37.760
- Oh, wow. - Hey.

405
28:37.898 --> 28:38.443
See?

406
28:38.669 --> 28:41.250
How come you didn’t know about this?

407
28:41.272 --> 28:42.272
Right.

408
28:42.690 --> 28:43.690
How did you not know?

409
28:44.145 --> 28:45.869
We need to stop eating egg yolk ice-cream.

410
28:48.310 --> 28:50.232
And you need to start eating vegetables, too.

411
28:50.269 --> 28:51.534
Don’t even try.

412
28:51.550 --> 28:52.981
Why don’t you have any vegetables on your plate?

413
28:53.003 --> 28:54.298
I don’t like vegetables.

414
28:54.312 --> 28:55.461
(Please, Ruth. Don’t even try.)

415
28:55.483 --> 28:57.460
(You haven’t touched the vegetables I gave you.)

416
28:57.767 --> 28:59.440
Both of you, stop being picky.

417
28:59.483 --> 29:01.309
You’re grownups. Just eat them.

418
29:04.830 --> 29:07.025
(There’s something I shouldn't forget.)

419
29:08.240 --> 29:09.454
(The fact that)

420
29:10.450 --> 29:11.869
(he's just a 17-year-old boy.)

421
29:22.494 --> 29:23.494
What’s the matter?

422
29:28.340 --> 29:29.340
Ji?

423
29:30.770 --> 29:33.149
Pim, what’s the penalty for abducting a minor?

424
29:33.340 --> 29:34.340
Huh?

425
29:37.890 --> 29:39.083
Hey, Pim.

426
29:40.380 --> 29:41.883
I'm going into town to buy something.

427
29:42.443 --> 29:43.443
Wanna come with me?

428
29:43.505 --> 29:44.505
Mm, okay.

429
29:45.670 --> 29:46.670
What about you guys?

430
29:46.800 --> 29:50.349
Ji and I have a mission today.

431
29:51.540 --> 29:52.385
A mission?

432
29:52.421 --> 29:53.421
What mission?

433
29:55.400 --> 29:56.400
It's a secret.

434
29:58.290 --> 30:00.087
- Fine. - Let’s go, Pim.

435
30:00.116 --> 30:00.821
See you.

436
30:00.865 --> 30:02.145
- Mm, see you. - See you.

437
30:07.860 --> 30:09.180
Ji, I have something to tell you.

438
30:11.498 --> 30:13.490
I'm going to audition for the lead role.

439
30:15.790 --> 30:18.960
I'm going to be a shining star in the sky,

440
30:18.996 --> 30:21.243
a bird soaring freely through the air.

441
30:22.967 --> 30:23.967
Huh?

442
30:25.236 --> 30:27.963
CASTING CALL DRAMA CLUB

443
30:28.420 --> 30:29.876
Hey Ji, Tyler.

444
30:32.270 --> 30:33.779
Ji, are you here for the audition, too?

445
30:33.803 --> 30:35.818
Oh, no. I’m just here to support.

446
30:36.050 --> 30:37.716
Tyler, do you have a scene partner yet?

447
30:38.683 --> 30:40.312
If not, want to rehearse together?

448
30:40.341 --> 30:41.120
So we won't waste any time.

449
30:41.360 --> 30:42.360
Okay, Ploy.

450
30:42.894 --> 30:44.036
I'll go get you the scripts.

451
30:48.210 --> 30:50.072
- Here you are. - Thanks.

452
30:50.305 --> 30:51.305
Have a seat.

453
30:52.810 --> 30:55.301
(Even though I wasn't interested in school activities, )

454
30:56.260 --> 30:58.269
(I remembered how much people talked)

455
30:58.298 --> 31:00.378
(about this school play in my previous life.)

456
31:00.407 --> 31:03.192
They're gonna make it in the entertainment industry for sure.

457
31:03.221 --> 31:05.272
It's not easy for just anyone to become an actor.

458
31:05.309 --> 31:08.276
But if you're as handsome and talented as President Ruth,

459
31:08.305 --> 31:09.305
then it's possible.

460
31:09.454 --> 31:10.130
That's true.

461
31:10.283 --> 31:13.389
This year's Drama Club lead actor has been getting a lot of attention.

462
31:13.738 --> 31:16.087
How about we sit near the front?

463
31:16.123 --> 31:18.203
That way, we can take pictures of President Ruth.

464
31:27.020 --> 31:29.020
Do you want to go inside the air-conditioned room?

465
31:29.840 --> 31:31.120
You're waiting for Tyler, right?

466
31:31.323 --> 31:32.472
You can wait inside.

467
31:32.720 --> 31:34.327
It's hot and noisy out here.

468
31:34.800 --> 31:36.320
But I'm not in the club.

469
31:36.910 --> 31:37.898
It's fine.

470
31:37.920 --> 31:39.621
I'm not asking you to be a judge.

471
31:40.380 --> 31:41.700
Just go in there and take a seat.

472
31:47.352 --> 31:49.350
The first audition starts in 10 minutes.

473
31:49.650 --> 31:50.650
So?

474
32:16.830 --> 32:17.396
Hey.

475
32:17.425 --> 32:18.930
Close that damn door already.

476
32:18.960 --> 32:20.280
The air conditioning is escaping.

477
32:27.770 --> 32:28.770
Um…

478
32:30.080 --> 32:31.080
This is Thiti.

479
32:31.134 --> 32:33.174
He writes the script for our school play every year.

480
32:34.390 --> 32:35.390
What?

481
32:35.614 --> 32:38.145
Do you think I just spend all my time at school and cram school

482
32:38.167 --> 32:39.727
and don't know how to do anything else?

483
32:42.429 --> 32:44.540
Hey, hey, hey. Do you think Thiti isn't qualified?

484
32:44.581 --> 32:45.665
No, no, no.

485
32:45.694 --> 32:47.425
- He’s perfect for this. - Perfect.

486
32:47.570 --> 32:48.705
- So amazing. - Amazing.

487
32:48.741 --> 32:49.854
Truly amazing.

488
32:50.203 --> 32:53.025
And this is Gun, the head of the set design team.

489
32:53.556 --> 32:55.330
You already know each other, right?

490
32:55.883 --> 32:57.330
You're both in Class 7.

491
32:57.740 --> 32:59.100
Everyone, this is Ji from Class 7.

492
32:59.469 --> 33:01.658
- He's here to help us out today. - Huh?

493
33:01.760 --> 33:02.821
We haven't decided on his role yet,

494
33:02.843 --> 33:04.538
but Lita recommended him.

495
33:04.560 --> 33:06.530
She said he's really good at coordinating things.

496
33:06.800 --> 33:07.454
Right, Ji?

497
33:07.767 --> 33:08.767
No.

498
33:34.174 --> 33:35.174
Fah.

499
33:35.629 --> 33:36.629
Romeo.

500
33:37.280 --> 33:38.938
Why art thou called Romeo?

501
33:56.930 --> 33:57.930
- Good luck. - Good luck.

502
34:03.490 --> 34:04.490
Ji!

503
34:10.660 --> 34:12.065
Hello.

504
34:49.861 --> 34:51.860
Thanks so much, everyone. That's all for today.

505
34:52.490 --> 34:55.898
Those of you staying for the rest of the auditions, take a 30-minute break.

506
34:55.912 --> 34:57.505
Grab something to eat, then come back.

507
34:57.534 --> 34:59.032
Thanks again for today.

508
35:11.640 --> 35:12.680
Ji, aren't you going home?

509
35:12.952 --> 35:14.152
Tyler will be waiting for you.

510
35:15.480 --> 35:17.127
Is this the only round of auditions?

511
35:17.447 --> 35:18.487
Will there be another one?

512
35:18.632 --> 35:19.632
No, this is it.

513
35:19.883 --> 35:20.883
Why do you ask?

514
35:21.910 --> 35:24.167
Isn't Ruth auditioning?

515
35:24.407 --> 35:25.883
Oh, Ruth.

516
35:26.980 --> 35:28.189
Don't mention that name again.

517
35:28.203 --> 35:29.265
I'm still bitter about it.

518
35:30.620 --> 35:31.620
Why?

519
35:31.658 --> 35:33.512
We'd talked about wanting

520
35:33.549 --> 35:35.736
our famous student council president to play the lead role.

521
35:35.760 --> 35:37.178
But he had to withdraw

522
35:37.207 --> 35:38.727
because he had student council duties.

523
35:39.876 --> 35:41.870
Then he recommended Tyler instead,

524
35:42.043 --> 35:44.872
in exchange for... getting us a meeting room to use.

525
35:48.090 --> 35:49.643
(What I feared most, )

526
35:50.341 --> 35:53.250
(Besides a relationship that should never happen, )

527
35:54.240 --> 35:57.687
(was that I might unknowingly ruin his bright future.)

528
36:03.870 --> 36:04.950
Have you been waiting long?

529
36:05.620 --> 36:06.620
I haven’t.

530
36:07.832 --> 36:09.447
Shall we go, then?

531
36:10.080 --> 36:13.258
My mom just called and said she'd prepared dinner for us.

532
36:50.180 --> 36:51.180
Ruth.

533
36:56.540 --> 36:58.189
I think we should break up.

534
37:04.370 --> 37:05.370
I’m sorry.

535
37:09.850 --> 37:10.850
It’s not because of you.

536
37:12.560 --> 37:13.665
About the school play,

537
37:14.600 --> 37:15.600
it was my own decision.

538
37:17.600 --> 37:18.727
Are you sure?

539
37:19.069 --> 37:20.952
I heard talent scouts will be there.

540
37:21.847 --> 37:24.952
You could become a nationally famous actor someday,

541
37:24.989 --> 37:26.472
with lots of money.

542
37:26.523 --> 37:29.243
- To be loved and admired by everyone. - That's not the life I want.

543
37:29.280 --> 37:30.327
How do you know?

544
37:30.647 --> 37:33.134
That's the ultimate dream for a lot of people.

545
37:33.163 --> 37:34.163
I know.

546
37:35.990 --> 37:36.990
I do.

547
37:43.730 --> 37:45.440
Because I have lived that life.

548
37:49.720 --> 37:50.720
What do you mean?

549
38:03.810 --> 38:05.054
Think about it.

550
38:07.530 --> 38:08.800
When did I start changing?

551
38:18.310 --> 38:19.310
Ji?

552
38:20.380 --> 38:21.380
Jiraphat?

553
38:21.607 --> 38:23.578
Why are you staring at me like that?

554
38:24.218 --> 38:26.414
Ms. Suda has been reported.

555
38:26.436 --> 38:27.621
Did it reach the principal?

556
38:27.650 --> 38:29.570
The complaint itself isn't the issue.

557
38:29.607 --> 38:32.407
The issue is who's behind it.

558
38:32.436 --> 38:35.436
- (Let's cross the overbridge.) - (We might not get another chance tomorrow.)

559
38:35.460 --> 38:37.592
The photo booth is what came back, not us.

560
38:54.065 --> 38:55.065
Since when?

561
38:59.840 --> 39:01.061
Not long after you did.

562
39:20.460 --> 39:21.505
Are you exhausted?

563
40:35.710 --> 40:38.610
(What do you think brought us here?)

564
40:39.745 --> 40:41.740
Romeo, do you love me?

565
40:42.312 --> 40:43.520
I swear by the moon.

566
40:43.760 --> 40:44.760
(Don't be afraid.)

567
40:45.229 --> 40:46.229
(From now on, )

568
40:46.712 --> 40:47.752
(wherever you go, )

569
40:48.480 --> 40:49.480
(I'll go with you.)

570
40:50.167 --> 40:51.410
Mr. President.

571
40:52.050 --> 40:53.530
What are you doing in the Drama Club?

572
40:55.745 --> 40:56.749
Why can’t I be here?

573
40:56.981 --> 40:58.669
(I want to do what we did on Sports Day.)
